  <div class="pl-cards">
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>common/UrlNormalizer.kt — add Article.computeNormalizedUrl() extension</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>New extension function placed after the existing <code>normalizeUrl(url: String)</code> top-level function. Delegates directly: <code>normalizeUrl(this.url ?: this.givenUrl ?: "")</code>. Zero behaviour change — output is byte-identical to the 4 inline expressions it replaces. If a circular-dependency check fails (common/ importing data/local/database/), move to <code>data/local/database/ArticleExt.kt</code> instead.</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "add", "text": "fun Article.computeNormalizedUrl(): String =" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "    normalizeUrl(this.url ?: this.givenUrl ?: \"\")" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>data/ArticleRepository.kt — replace 1 Article-typed call site (line 172)</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>Replaces the inline null-coalescing expression in <code>add(articleData)</code> with the extension. The <code>normalizeUrl</code> import is removed if this is the only call; <code>computeNormalizedUrl</code> import is added.</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "normalizedUrl = normalizeUrl(datum.article.url ?: datum.article.givenUrl ?: \"\")," },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "normalizedUrl = datum.article.computeNormalizedUrl()," }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>services/firestore/FirestoreSyncManager.kt — replace 2 Article-typed call sites (lines 89, 106)</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>Both occurrences inside <code>handleRemoteArticleChange()</code> — new-article insert path and conflict-resolution update path — use the identical expression; both replaced with <code>remoteArticle.computeNormalizedUrl()</code>.</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "normalizedUrl = normalizeUrl(remoteArticle.url ?: remoteArticle.givenUrl ?: \"\")" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "normalizedUrl = remoteArticle.computeNormalizedUrl()" },
          { "kind": "ctx", "text": "// (same replacement applied at both line 89 and line 106)" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>screens/articleList/ArticleListViewModel.kt — replace 1 Article-typed call site (line 264); 3 string-typed calls unchanged</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>Only the <code>insertArticle(article)</code> call at line 264 is Article-typed and replaced. The three calls at lines 318/376/436 operate on already-resolved URL strings (post-unfurl) and are intentionally left as <code>normalizeUrl(resolvedUrl)</code> — the <code>normalizeUrl</code> import is retained for them.</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "normalizedUrl = normalizeUrl(article.url ?: article.givenUrl ?: \"\")" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "normalizedUrl = article.computeNormalizedUrl()" },
          { "kind": "ctx", "text": "// normalizeUrl import kept — still used at lines 318/376/436 for String args" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>test/common/UrlNormalizerTest.kt — add Article extension parity cases</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>4 new test cases asserting <code>article.computeNormalizedUrl() == normalizeUrl(article.url ?: article.givenUrl ?: "")</code>: (1) url non-null, (2) url null / givenUrl fallback, (3) both non-null (url wins), (4) both null (graceful empty). Existing 16 cases are untouched.</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "add", "text": "@Test fun `computeNormalizedUrl uses url when present`() { ... }" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "@Test fun `computeNormalizedUrl falls back to givenUrl`() { ... }" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "@Test fun `computeNormalizedUrl url wins over givenUrl`() { ... }" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "@Test fun `computeNormalizedUrl both null returns empty`() { ... }" }
        ] } -->
